-- title:
--   Vertical height-one primes of the j-integral closure
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$, and let $K$ be a finite-dimensional intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$. Work at level $1\cdot q$ and write $C =$ `jIntegralClosure (1*q) A K` for the subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$-Laurent series consisting of those elements of `fieldOver (1*q) K` — the subfield generated by the constant series from $K$ together with $j$ and its level-$q$ expansion `jqModC`, `jqNModC (1*q)` — that are integral over `jRing A K`, the subring generated by the constant series from `coeffSubring A K` and `jqModC`. Let $\mathfrak p \subset C$ be a prime ideal of height $1$ containing the image of the natural number $q$. Let $g$ be an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1*q)`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of the Laurent series field generated by the coefficient embedding of the full modular function field of level $q$, and assume: $g$ lies in `fieldOver (1*q) K`; and both $g$ and its image under the base-changed Fricke automorphism `frickeInvolutionBar (1*q)` lie in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1*q) A.toSubring red`, i.e. each can be written as $r/s$ with $r,s$ in the subring generated by the constant series from $A$ and by `jqModC`, `jqNModC (1*q)` and with $s$ outside the prime ideal `redKer` cut out by reduction along $\mathrm{red}$. The conclusion is that there are $r,s \in C$ with $s \notin \mathfrak p$ and $g\,s = r$ as Laurent series; that is, $g$ lies in the localisation $C_{\mathfrak p}$.
--
--   This is the vertical half of the height-one analysis of the integral closure $C$: the height-one primes of $C$ containing $q$ are the generic points of the components of the special fibre at $q$, and absence of a vertical pole is expressed by membership in the two Gauss-type rings attached to $g$ and to its Fricke transform. It feeds the node-localised study of $X_0(q)$ in characteristic $q$, being cited by [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.exists_heightOne_mem_of_mul_eq_of_not_isUnit_frobNodePair`](thm.html#ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.exists_heightOne_mem_of_mul_eq_of_not_isUnit_frobNodePair), [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.ne_zero_of_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_forall_centred_ord_eq_zero_of_mem_ssJSet`](thm.html#ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.ne_zero_of_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_forall_centred_ord_eq_zero_of_mem_ssJSet) and [`ModularCurve.exists_mul_eq_of_height_one_of_forall_pole_not_centred`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_mul_eq_of_height_one_of_forall_pole_not_centred).
